# ── MON-87 migration image (docker/migration/Dockerfile) ────────────────────────
# The stock flyway/flyway base bundles JDBC drivers for databases MONTEIS does not use
# (SQL Server, Couchbase, GCP Spanner/BigQuery, Databricks, ...). Those unused drivers
# under /flyway/drivers + their shaded jackson / guava / httpcore5 / lz4 jars carry HIGH
# CVEs for code paths the Postgres-only migration Job never loads. We waive them by id here
# CVEs in the Postgres driver, the flyway engine (/flyway/lib), the JRE, or the OS are
# deliberately NOT listed and still fail the gate.
# Re-audit this list whenever the flyway base image digest is bumped.
# Last audit: flyway/flyway 13.13.0-alpine (2026-11-26) — every id below only hits
# jars under /flyway/drivers; ids no longer present were removed.
#
# com.microsoft.sqlserver:mssql-jdbc (SQL Server driver)
CVE-2025-59250
# org.apache.httpcomponents.core5:httpcore5 / httpcore5-h2 (shaded in databricks-jdbc)
CVE-2026-54399
CVE-2026-54428
# jackson SHADED inside databricks-jdbc (2.18.8) and couchbase core-io (2.21.6).
# flyway's own jackson in 13.13.0 (/flyway/lib: 2.22.4 / 3.1.8) is not affected,
# so these ids only hit the unused drivers
CVE-2026-68497
CVE-2026-89407
CVE-2026-89425
CVE-2026-91776
CVE-2026-91777
# at.yawk.lz4:lz4-java 1.10.1 (shaded in databricks-jdbc)
CVE-2026-106451
# com.google.guava:guava — standalone in drivers/gcp (Spanner/BigQuery), shaded inside
# databricks-jdbc (33.0.0) and couchbase core-io (33.4.0). No guava on the Postgres
# migration path
CVE-2026-102554
